  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "[stacks-project]",
  "statement": "In a commutative triangle $T\\to Y\\to B$, if $T\\to B$ is proper and\n$Y\\to B$ is separated, then $T\\to Y$ is proper.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-common/lemma-nagata-proper-to-separated-target.md",
    "place": "node lemma-nagata-proper-to-separated-target, order 237"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "Factor $T\\to Y$ through the graph\n$T\\to T\\times_BY$. The graph is closed because $Y\\to B$ is separated, and\nthe projection $T\\times_BY\\to Y$ is the base change of the proper morphism\n$T\\to B$.",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    }
